# Godot MCP (required when possible)

This is a **Godot 4.7+** project. Prefer the **`user-godot`** MCP tools over hand-editing `.tscn`/project files or raw CLI when a tool covers the task.

## Prefer MCP for

| Task | Tool |
|------|------|
| Version / project metadata | `get_godot_version`, `get_project_info`, `list_projects` |
| Open editor | `launch_editor` |
| Create / edit scenes & nodes | `create_scene`, `add_node`, `save_scene`, `load_sprite` |
| Run / stop / debug output | `run_project`, `stop_project`, `get_debug_output` |
| UIDs (4.4+) | `get_uid`, `update_project_uids` |

Always pass `projectPath` as the workspace root (`/home/jura/greenhouse` or `.`).

## When MCP is not enough

- GDScript / `.gd` logic, Resources (`.tres`), autoloads config: edit files directly.
- After meaningful scene or gameplay changes, **`run_project`** and check `get_debug_output`.
- For architecture, composition, performance, or visual QA, follow the **godot-master** skill.

## Do not

- Invent scene XML by hand when `create_scene` / `add_node` can do it.
- Leave a running game session hanging — call `stop_project` when done testing.
